  "which_population": "The probe found 53,778 notable and factless features by class alone. The gate diagnostic counts 40,123, because the script tests class, country and market BEFORE it tests notable and measurable. 40,123 is the correct population for yield.",
  "verdict": "REAL BUT MODEST. Enrichment recovers roughly 7,900 own pages at the two fact bar, not the 40,123 upper bound I carried into the ceiling table. At a one fact bar it would be roughly 29,800, but lowering the bar to one fact is relaxing a quality gate and is not done.",
  "caveat": "Some gained values are Wikidata entity URIs, for example heritage designation Q1188447, and have to be resolved to a readable label before they are a fact on a page. They are counted here as gained because the statement exists, and resolving labels is work, not a blocker.",
  "mean_is_low": "A mean of 1.04 facts per entity says Wikidata is thin for exactly the entities OSM is thin for. The two sources are correlated, not complementary, which is itself the finding: there is no large hidden reserve of facts behind the notability flag."
